    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Programs of Graduate Study in the Basic Biological Sciences"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.0, 457.964, 383.802, 529.077 ],
    "font" : "PalatinoLinotype-Roman",
    "font size" : 7.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The Division of the Biological Sciences offers a variety of graduate programs leading to the Ph.D. degree. Graduate programs are offered under the aegis of divisional departments as well as interdepartmental committees composed of faculty members with a common interest in a broad but definable area of advanced study. Some programs are organized into larger groups called clusters, a structure that provides cohesion across programs through shared retreats, common curriculum, and shared administrative duties. A few programs offer unique training opportunities and are not organized into a cluster. Joint programs also may be devised in other divisions of the university, such as with chemistry in the Division of the Physical Sciences and psychology in the Division of the Social Sciences. The fundamentals of graduate education in the division are not altered by these provisions. Students complete their degree in individual graduate programs."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.0, 428.964, 378.363, 452.077 ],
    "font" : "PalatinoLinotype-Roman",
    "font size" : 7.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The University’s hallmark emphasis on interdisciplinary research and collaboration, coupled with access to the latest technology and to three major affiliated laboratories, offers the opportunity to enrich human life in Chicago and around the globe through basic, translational, and clinical research."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 36.0, 383.964, 381.037, 423.077 ],
    "font" : "PalatinoLinotype-Roman",
    "font size" : 7.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The goal of the programs is the creation and dissemination of fundamental knowledge of life processes and the education and training of outstanding young scholars in these disciplines. To this end, the Division of the Biological Sciences has assembled a dedicated and talented faculty, strong in research and teaching, and has developed laboratory and other facilities of the first rank that allow the faculty and graduate students to pursue their goals at the highest level of excellence."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 50.4, 357.964, 355.6, 378.077 ],
